  "caveats": [
    "Students are simulated. These numbers show the system behaves as designed under stated assumptions; they are not evidence of learning gains in real students.",
    "World assumption: a question is answered correctly (up to slip) only if the concept and all its direct prerequisites are known, and a concept is learned from practice ten times more slowly while a prerequisite is missing. The learner model makes the same structural assumption, which favours it over baselines.",
    "Simulated slip, guess, learning and forgetting rates differ per student and are hidden from the model, but the model's fixed parameters were chosen by us with this kind of world in mind.",
    "Mastery is a binary hidden state per concept; real knowledge is graded.",
    "Pramana's repetition rate of zero is a property of the selector, not a discovery: it never serves a seen question while an unseen one exists in scope. Here the bank holds 12 questions per concept; the product generates new ones on demand.",
    "Misconception detection from distractor choice alone was unreliable at this data volume (see recall and precision columns). 'Observable' is the share of seeded misconceptions whose concept drew two or more wrong answers, an upper bound on recall."
  ]
}